{"c":[{"id":"04ad6c4e13eff575","sum":"Full pytest drops torch via test_coverage_collection make coverage-engine exact sync. Later: No module named torch.distributed; ensure-env, then rerun. Zstd check: filter persistent or no .wal. Replayed rows persistent=false Uncompressed; persistent segments are ZSTD.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261023T144151Z-19beeb928bb79a4a","text":"Measured 2026-10-23: a bare full pytest run in a torch-provisioned checkout drops torch midway: test_coverage_collection runs make coverage-engine, whose sync is exact. Later torch-gated tests fail (No module named torch.distributed); ensure-env, then rerun them.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T152930Z-94e11b6c634d81a7","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0, measured 2026-10-23: a zstd-column file opened read-only with a .wal (killed ingest) lists the replayed rows in pragma_storage_info as persistent=false, Uncompressed; every persistent segment is ZSTD. A zstd check must filter persistent or run with no .wal.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c67ab4511ba06727","sum":"pytest --ignore=tests/test_coverage_collection.py keeps torch; only that module make coverage-engine exact sync removes it. Puck step 8.4 at 09ea4ae exited 0 in 43s: shadow copy stayed v1.0.0+, schema head, no index. DuckDB 1.5.4 wrote it and 2.0.0 read it. Live inode unchanged.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261023T154646Z-7f876ab5674122fe","text":"QA 2026-10-23: in a torch-provisioned live checkout, pytest --ignore=tests/test_coverage_collection.py runs the rest of the suite and keeps torch; only that module's make coverage-engine runs the exact sync that removes it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T164313Z-a987fa985b63d02d","text":"Puck step 8.4 at 09ea4ae exited 0 in 43s: shadow copy stayed v1.0.0+, schema head, no index. DuckDB 1.5.4 wrote it and 2.0.0 read it. Live warehouse inode unchanged.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
